34,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The fixed costs are higher than I expected, totaling over 280,000 yen. Also, the diary shows a huge disparity in usage, with Saturdays being far busier than Tuesdays.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"My research suggests that the social friction often stems from the burden of asking favors or clinging to unnecessary turns, and that auditing each other's figures can create a climate of accusation.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"It's exactly as I feared. The car is often handed over with the fuel light on or full of rubbish, and our weekly repeating trips are the ones most likely to collapse.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The fuel receipts are completely lopsided; two of us paid for over half the fuel while one barely contributed. Also, recording every run for a month took nearly an hour a week.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I found that heavy use comes in bursts, like house moves, which takes up whole evenings of planning. Also, the mechanic said short cold runs are wearing out the brakes and battery faster.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minako,,"It seems we are all subsidizing different things—some in money, some in time, and some in patience. We cannot simply split everything equally if the usage is this uneven.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, you've hit the nail on the head. If we focus solely on the financial split, we risk exacerbating the social tension I discovered; the feeling of being ""accused"" is a dangerous catalyst.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"I'm less concerned with the social tension and more with the practical failure. If the car is dirty and empty, the system is broken regardless of who is paying for what.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"Exactly. The ""broken system"" is a result of the guesswork. If we don't have a strict way to track usage and payments, we'll just keep having these lopsided fuel contributions.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,I just... I don't want us to spend an hour a week recording every single run like Shion mentioned. That sounds like it would just add more stress to the evenings we're already spending planning.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minako,,"We need a system that balances fairness with simplicity. If detailed tracking is too burdensome, we must find a middle ground that doesn't leave some of us paying for everyone else.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Perhaps a system that reduces the need for constant negotiation and ""favors"" would be best. We should avoid anything that feels like a police state of auditing each other's every move.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"I agree with Benjamin. We need a system where the car is simply available when it's supposed to be, without me having to hope the previous driver was considerate.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"If we avoid tracking, we're just choosing to stay in the dark. We can't fix the fuel imbalance or the usage gaps without some form of accountability.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I just think we should avoid anything that makes us feel like we're fighting over every single kilometer. Maybe there's a way to be fair without it being so... intense.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minako,,"We have a clear picture now: high fixed costs, uneven usage, social friction, and poor maintenance. We must choose a system that addresses these without creating more conflict.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I agree. We must weigh the need for accountability against the risk of resentment. Let us see which of the proposed options can resolve these contradictions most elegantly.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"I just want a solution that guarantees the car is ready for me on my specific days, regardless of who used it last. Reliability is my priority.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,"Reliability is fine, but it doesn't pay the bills. We need a system that ensures the financial burden is distributed based on actual use, not just hope and good intentions.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I just want something that doesn't require us to spend our whole evening arguing or planning. If we can find a way to make it simple and quiet, I'd be happy.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
