59,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Minako,,"We have three options: A, a fixed day allocation with a monthly share; B, a booking calendar with costs divided by distance; or C, a primary keeper who manages the car.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option A seems the most elegant for reducing social friction, as it eliminates the need for constant favors and the resentment of auditing each other's figures.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option A is the only one that guarantees the car is available for my weekly trips without the risk of them collapsing at short notice. I vote for A.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shion,,Option A is too vague on costs. Option B is the only one that ensures the fuel imbalance is corrected by charging based on actual distance. I vote for B.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,I'm worried Option B would just lead to more of that recording and calculating we all hate. Option A sounds much quieter. I vote for A.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minako,,"Option A provides a stable structure, but Option C could relieve the planning burden Daisuke mentioned. However, for overall stability and fairness, I also vote for A.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Shion, while B is precise, the data shows that auditing figures creates a climate of accusation. A provides a clean break from that cycle. I vote for A.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,I've already cast my vote for A. It solves the reliability issue and the handover chaos by giving us clear ownership of specific days.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shion,,"You're all prioritizing peace over precision. If we go with A, we're just guessing again and hoping the monthly share is ""fair"" enough. I'll stick with B.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I agree with Benjamin. I can't handle the stress of tracking every kilometer. I'm staying with my vote for A.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minako,,"It seems the consensus is leaning heavily toward Option A. While Shion's desire for precision is logical, the social and mental cost of Option B appears too high for the rest of us.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely. The goal is a sustainable living arrangement, not a perfect accounting ledger. A system that preserves our relationships is far more valuable than one that saves a few yen.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"I agree. If we can avoid the constant stress of negotiating and the disappointment of a missing car, the fixed share is a small price to pay.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shion,,"Fine. If the majority prefers a comfortable illusion of fairness over actual accuracy, I can't stop you. I'll accept the result, but don't complain when the costs feel uneven.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I'm just glad we can agree on something that doesn't make us fight. I'm okay with Option A.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minako,,"The vote is clear. With four votes for Option A and one for Option B, we will adopt the Fixed Day Allocation. Let's now decide which days each of us will take.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"A most satisfactory conclusion. I look forward to a future where our conversations are about our lives, rather than the logistics of a combustion engine.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I'm just relieved. I'll make sure my assigned days are locked in so my morning routine finally becomes predictable.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shion,,"I'll go along with it. Just make sure the ""fixed monthly share"" is calculated using the actual fixed costs Minako found, not another guess.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'll do that. I'm just happy we can finally stop the arguing and have some peace.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
